# THE UNDERSLUNG GRENADE LAUNCHER'S TUBE -- NOT THIS GUN'S ACTION (2026-10-02).
#
# It carried `role = action`, which is what gives a gun its CYCLE verb, so RACKING THIS
# MACHINE GUN SLID THE GRENADE LAUNCHER'S TUBE FORWARD. The role also earned it
# `detach = 0.95` from the emitter (a behaviour default per role, not a measurement), so
# pulling the tube far enough took the launcher off the gun. One cause, both faults.
#
# The M249's own bolt is not a separate surface in this donor, so there is nothing here
# to rack at all. The tube opens instead, exactly as Vanilla's WM_MachineGun cards this
# same part map (WMCARD.09_chaingun) -- and that is what BD's own reload shows: the
# ReloadGrenade state plays GRLLO1, insertshell, GRLLO2 (Machinegun.txt:222-236).
part launchertube
  subject = foregrip
  surface = launchertube
  grab       = 39.128, -0.310, -6.667
  grabradius = 3.0
  dof
    kind     = slide
    axis     = 1.000, -0.000, -0.000
    distance = 9.504
  end
end

# THE BREECH: the tube slides forward and the latch frees it. No `from` -- this verb
# throws nothing, because this card declares no grenade store.
#
# WHY NOT THE WHOLE LAUNCHER. Vanilla's WM_MachineGun carries a `store gl`, a
# `load grenade` and a `barrel launcher` on altfire, and this gun's donor has all of it
# (Machinegun.txt AltFire fires ShortGrenade off AmmoRocket, one at a time). It is not
# carded here because A CARD HAS ONE magfamily and this gun already spends it: unlike
# Vanilla's, this machine gun has a carved 7.62 magazine a hand swaps. Vanilla's is
# reserve-fed, so a grenade is the only thing a hand ever brings it and "40mm" costs it
# nothing. Carding the grenade here would stop the 7.62 magazine fitting -- trading a
# reload that works for one that does not. The grenade still fires: BD's own AltFire
# drives it, untouched.
open breech
  part        = launchertube
  latch       = launcherlatch
  latchreturn = spring
  openat      = 0.85
  closeat     = 0.05
  rest        = stay
end

# THE MAGAZINE SWAP, WRITTEN DOWN BECAUSE THE OPEN VERB ABOVE TOOK IT AWAY.
#
# SynthesiseVerbs is all or nothing: `if (verbs.Size() > 0 || mechanism != "") return;`
# (card.zs:918). This card had no verbs, so it was handed a synthesised swap on its
# `role = feed` part. Declaring the breech gave it one verb, which stopped the synthesis
# -- and the magazine kept its role, so a hand could still take it and nothing would
# happen. The load log says so out loud: "part magazine is role = feed and no verb works
# it". That line is how this was caught; it is worth reading on every card.
#
# These are SynthSwap's own numbers (verb.zs:350-364), not new ones: id magwell, the
# facade's counted store, detachat from the part's own dof (0.9), pullout 0.97, button
# yes, handtake from the part's `take = no`. seatat is left unstated so it keeps reading
# wm_seat_at live, as the synthesised verb did.
swap magwell
  part     = magazine
  store    = mag
  detachat = 0.9
  pullout  = 0.97
  button   = yes
  handtake = no
end

part launchertrigger
  surface = launchertrigger
  grab       = -1.952, -0.317, -9.429
  grabradius = 2.0
  dof
    kind     = hinge
    axis     = 0.000, 1.000, 0.000
    degrees  = 20.02
    pivot    = -2.193, 0.000, -7.863
  end
end

part launcherlatch
  surface = launcherlatch
  grab       = 0.860, -0.322, -9.276
  grabradius = 2.0
  dof
    kind     = hinge
    axis     = 0.000, -1.000, -0.000
    degrees  = 19.09
    pivot    = 0.777, 0.000, -8.250
  end
end

